8312	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s4","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s4-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-21T09:10:27.150Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Storing round content through the existing updateContent preserves earlier round outcomes in the log and satisfies ac12.","evidence":"DEF ac12 requires an entry 'with the round's outcome, so earlier rounds can still be read'. LifecycleService.updateContent supplies only `options: { operation: 'update' }`. ArtifactStore constructs entries with revision number/hash and includes outcome only when `options.outcome !== undefined`; it stores neither the old payload nor the new payload in the entry. The proposed three-argument RoundWriter cannot supply an outcome. Creating the first round without logging also leaves that round unavailable after its replacement. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Specify how round outcomes enter the staged ChangeLogEntry, including preservation of the first overwritten round. Extend the writer contract or explicitly derive the outcome inside the queued mutation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current recovery can overwrite a moved head, and the current TESTS writer restores its prior JSON when markdown writing fails.","evidence":"completePending appends a missing entry, then executes `if (current !== op.bytes) ...writeHead...(path, op.bytes)` without checking the prior head. persistTestRecordTask captures priorJson, writes JSON before markdown, and restores priorJson or removes the new JSON in its markdown-failure catch. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed recovery conflict check and the explicitly scoped rollback behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Durable sidecar and journal implementations are new work behind existing ports; the proposed RoundWriter shape already exists in the completion hook.","evidence":"sidecar.ts defines SidecarIo, createMemorySidecar and an unframed appendSidecarLine; journal.ts defines WriteJournal and createMemoryJournal. Searches found no production durable implementations. ensureBuildRecordOnCompletion already accepts `{ writer: BuildContentWriter; actor: Actor }`, where updateContent takes id, actor and HeadPayload and returns Promise<boolean>. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts]","action":"Reuse these ports and consolidate the existing completion-hook writer type.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Supplying RoundWriter from the code-review step handler covers production CR record persistence.","evidence":"The daemon also registers `codeReview.run` through codeReviewRunStart. src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts calls runCodeReview directly in degraded, injected-write and default branches; the default branch supplies no dependencies. The step handler routes daemon reviews to this RPC. This production writer is absent from the design's registry and RoundWriter change-site inventories, so those reviews retain the explicitly unchanged no-through finalize path. [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"Add codeReviewRunStart and its dependency contract to the change sites. Supply the repository RoundWriter in every runner branch and test both daemon and controller review routes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing heads without sidecars can pass lifecycle integrity checks with empty history.","evidence":"checkIntegrity returns `{ ok: true }` when `logTail?.revision === undefined`, after checking the head's own hash. LifecycleService.inspect and apply select the last revision-bearing entry, which is undefined for an empty log. Thus the proposed missing-file-as-empty reader preserves this compatibility, provided the head itself is valid. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"Keep an integration fixture with an existing valid head and no sidecars.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Durable lifecycle wiring and prior-head recovery checks are assigned to s4 rather than unauthorized extensions into s2 or s3.","evidence":"The HLD assigns physical sidecar storage and recovery to s4. AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-8 has `status: 'approved'` and adds s4 as an sc4 consumer for durable LifecycleService wiring. core-data-model.md explicitly assigns 'Recovery conflict (s4)' and staging the expected prior-head hash to s4. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/HLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-8.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"Retain these ownership references; leave lifecycle transition rules and Task build-history semantics with their designated stories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"An oversized entry rejected by appendRecord can be recovered simply by shortening the outcome and retrying.","evidence":"ArtifactStore calls `journal.stage` before `history.appendLog`. Subsequent writes and updates execute completePending first, which retries the immutable staged entry. The proposed size check occurs only at appendRecord, so an oversized entry becomes a permanently failing pending operation; a shorter replacement cannot reach staging. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts]","action":"Validate serialized entry size before staging, using the same framing validator as appendRecord. Specify recovery for already-staged invalid entries and test that a rejected oversized operation does not block a later valid write.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s4 acceptance criterion has a named proving test in the design.","evidence":"The DEF assigns ac11 to merging appended history/feedback, ac12 to preserving round outcomes, and ac13 to head conflicts. The design maps these to two-clone merge/read tests, round-recording tests and head-conflict/recovery tests respectively. The existing store-kit supplies stage, append, replace and clear fault injection suitable for the proposed recovery matrix. This verifies test-plan coverage, not execution or passing results. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S004/LLD.md, src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/store-kit.ts]","action":"Make ac12 assertions inspect actual historical outcomes across multiple replacements, and add the omitted daemon CR route and oversized-staging regression cases identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-21T09:10:27.150Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
